WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.584
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Meet Your Brain.

00:00:12.584 --> 00:00:17.168
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:17.168 --> 00:00:19.918
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:19.918 --> 00:00:22.669
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:22.669 --> 00:00:30.920
Today we meet your brain — the part of you that feels, and thinks, and learns.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:39.171
Here is one way to picture it. Your brain has a feeling part, and a thinking part.

00:00:39.171 --> 00:00:44.671
It is a picture that helps us — a simple way to imagine something we cannot see.

00:00:44.671 --> 00:00:48.338
Both parts are helpers. Both parts are yours. And both are working right now.

00:00:48.338 --> 00:00:57.506
The feeling part is warm and fast. It notices feelings first — joy, worry, mad, sad.

00:00:57.506 --> 00:01:03.924
Sometimes the feeling part gets loud, like a drum in your chest. That is its job: to tell you something matters.

00:01:03.924 --> 00:01:12.175
Picture a warm light glowing. That is your feeling part, doing its work.

00:01:12.175 --> 00:01:21.343
A loud feeling part is not bad. It is a helper, asking to be heard.

00:01:21.343 --> 00:01:31.427
The thinking part is cool and steady. It counts. It breathes. It finds words.

00:01:31.427 --> 00:01:36.928
When the feeling part is loud, we can give the thinking part a job.

00:01:36.928 --> 00:01:43.345
Try it now: count slowly in your mind — one, two, three, four.

00:01:43.345 --> 00:01:48.846
Feel the cool light glow a little. The thinking part is on the job.

00:01:48.846 --> 00:01:55.264
Warm light, cool light. Feeling and thinking, side by side. That is your whole brain, helping.

00:01:55.264 --> 00:02:02.598
All day, you can ask: which part feels loud right now? Then give the other part a job.

00:02:02.598 --> 00:02:05.348
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:05.348 --> 00:02:09.015
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:09.015 --> 00:02:12.682
You're ready for what's next.
